 "Research method", "children": [{"id": "365f39fb-5f9b-4356-a39f-142c72a2976a", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue spotting"}, {"id": "82dc0512-1f6c-4173-8609-a7444adbb789", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary versus secondary sources"}, {"id": "f6d7cf9d-388d-460a-aa61-f6335a4b8031", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax memo format and citation"}], "description": "Good tax answers begin with facts, issues, authority, analysis, and conclusion."}]}, {"id": "7b6a1fd9-676f-4ac8-a5f1-8187762dd7bf", "type": "topic", "title": "Entity Classification, C Corporation Formation, and Capital Structure", "description": "This topic explains when a business is taxed as a corporation and how property, stock, debt, and basis work at formation.", "children": [{"id": "906e5706-20dd-4fe8-98fd-304a6024e7eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Entity classification", "children": [{"id": "c571ae89-4791-44fc-9ebd-4baff88a1909", "type": "concept", "title": "Check-the-box rules"}, {"id": "f5f80e19-be9f-4f0d-80aa-96065e5024b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Per se corporations"}, {"id": "31867495-59aa-481e-827a-d020ee23fea7", "type": "concept", "title": "LLCs taxed as corporations or partnerships"}], "description": "Students learn why classification determines the tax regime."}, {"id": "10f2a7d0-df6f-4737-b090-cf84d9168dea", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Section 351 formation", "children": [{"id": "c3bd932c-8088-4386-a3f7-d45835ac694a", "type": "concept", "title": "Control requirement"}, {"id": "8275ab0b-e8df-4b53-84d4-3f90be73f6a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Property transfers"}, {"id": "eb8a8258-a60e-44ac-b6ee-14d583a425bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Boot and liabilities"}], "description": "Formation rules explain when incorporation can occur without immediate gain recognition."}, {"id": "be0b17f9-74b1-411d-9205-088dc73e5397", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capital structure", "children": [{"id": "f37c68ab-c8ab-48e7-86d3-412984cfcba9", "type": "concept", "title": "Stock basis"}, {"id": "621d87a3-0ee8-4714-8218-e4fa5f555042", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt versus equity"}, {"id": "601de614-3063-4967-b515-f8733a366a7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Thin capitalization and interest limits preview"}], "description": "Debt and equity classification affects deductions, basis, and shareholder returns."}]}, {"id": "8f9e5aee-e171-46b4-a3c2-b3b34faa9b14", "type": "topic", "title": "Corporate Taxable Income, Deductions, Credits, and Tax Accounting", "description": "Students learn how a C corporation computes taxable income and reconciles book, tax, timing, and method differences.", "children": [{"id": "e3f1d6a7-7236-443a-bfdf-a49122728d54", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Taxable income computation", "children": [{"id": "0c2efaaf-b89d-447f-8df7-eb673765c3c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Gross income"}, {"id": "195b6baf-ac38-4197-8eae-cb405f890267", "type": "concept", "title": "Ordinary and necessary business deductions"}, {"id": "98289399-3604-4eb7-9eec-35a924948fea", "type": "concept", "title": "Book-tax adjustments"}], "description": "Students connect book records to federal taxable income."}, {"id": "3afadd9c-c2ef-4bb4-aa48-2af90d8deefd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deductions and limitations", "children": [{"id": "f002bf1c-3cfb-4323-99b1-64fa30bbe406", "type": "concept", "title": "Depreciation and amortization"}, {"id": "79a60628-a3cc-4087-a2bd-9e38aba46453", "type": "concept", "title": "Net operating losses"}, {"id": "0fe2f2b8-e1a4-4f60-9321-52036dfce8a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Business interest expense limitation"}], "description": "Corporate deductions often depend on timing, policy, and anti-abuse limits."}, {"id": "f09fa44e-2b68-4d56-a281-af05e08cd1b5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tax accounting methods", "children": [{"id": "4b7bcf27-2a70-4833-a965-210f9d7c705f", "type": "concept", "title": "Accrual versus cash method"}, {"id": "69f62979-f769-460e-b2b4-cf1c3ca758e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory and capitalization"}, {"id": "91287ff3-1207-49f4-a1b3-00fa7b45bbeb", "type": "concept", "title": "Accounting method changes"}], "description": "Method and period rules determine when income and deductions appear."}]}, {"id": "59a96b17-b8cc-4f8c-91b1-d790e73df14b", "type": "topic", "title": "Earnings and Profits, Dividends, and Corporate Distributions", "description": "This module covers how corporate distributions are characterized and taxed to corporations and shareholders.", "children": [{"id": "fe2c13ad-d616-4cd0-8572-2d64f64f142a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Earnings and profits", "children": [{"id": "71e2c5df-2cf5-47a1-ae6b-ee35ff919fe7", "type": "concept", "title": "Current E&P"}, {"id": "812497d8-922b-470e-ba2a-d5df44020200", "type": "concept", "title": "Accumulated E&P"}, {"id": "7b723ae3-1c89-4f7c-8a2f-3f8d4232539d", "type": "concept", "title": "Adjustments from taxable income"}], "description": "E&P measures corporate capacity to make taxable dividends."}, {"id": "50b767dc-65f1-4c2c-897e-fc5bc7fadd48", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Distribution ordering", "children": [{"id": "f6c32325-64c3-4582-906f-4535d553e96c", "type": "concept", "title": "Dividend to extent of E&P"}, {"id": "f0e34c3b-6dfd-4dfe-b52f-3c37eb7271b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Return of basis"}, {"id": "d9d003e8-c452-460e-942a-7c66957bec8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital gain after basis recovery"}], "description": "Students learn how distributions are classified to shareholders."}, {"id": "3495b431-3cea-46c4-846f-c703ffd8bdc2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Corporate consequences", "children": [{"id": "ef40ec44-5a0e-4a65-8b96-db8fff56ba86", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 311(b)"}, {"id": "ad5fd91c-9ff1-4973-8d6b-03e4a9be4183", "type": "concept", "title": "Liability assumptions"}, {"id": "93769a0e-3373-4c4e-a0c6-c4bb0264869b", "type": "concept", "title": "Property basis and fair market value"}], "description": "Distributing appreciated property can trigger corporate-level tax."}]}, {"id": "dd386db1-df81-490a-8b8d-6f37ab1ae032", "type": "topic", "title": "Redemptions, Stock Buybacks, and Shareholder-Level Consequences", "description": "Students learn when a redemption is treated like a sale and when it is taxed as a dividend.", "children": [{"id": "3ebf4a37-3d35-4cce-9347-49c1b993c5c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sale versus dividend treatment", "children": [{"id": "7c515b75-cfcd-40e4-a3a3-4f9ee2fdd190", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 302 tests"}, {"id": "833afc89-186e-4f61-90c7-d24afdbce709", "type": "concept", "title": "Substantially disproportionate redemption"}, {"id": "363acf48-d43e-411b-84b3-c0bb369ae6d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Complete termination"}], "description": "Redemption rules determine whether the shareholder receives exchange treatment."}, {"id": "90f8691f-f6be-49b0-9901-ea44f14f8902", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Attribution rules", "children": [{"id": "7c7085e9-1b71-4f4f-acd7-edda4d5487f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Family attribution"}, {"id": "836bdd86-a98e-4801-aa69-ccae36e09601", "type": "concept", "title": "Entity attribution"}, {"id": "e21d87c0-d159-4ed8-b552-65a3e073cbf6", "type": "concept", "title": "Waiver rules"}], "description": "Constructive ownership can defeat sale treatment."}, {"id": "39e6a8e7-f23d-4ad3-b574-a13865d880f9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planning and compliance", "children": [{"id": "5d2fa807-d63d-40e3-bc66-b47cf5d8267d", "type": "concept", "title": "Basis recovery"}, {"id": "52ee1885-d36e-434f-a522-8186817ae172", "type": "concept", "title": "E&P effects"}, {"id": "05f91634-76a0-4f8b-bf6f-c5b4f4facb13", "type": "concept", "title": "Reporting and disclosure"}], "description": "Students learn how buybacks create tax, control, and documentation issues."}]}, {"id": "19398cee-cf81-4b0c-ac8e-46af86c2099c", "type": "topic", "title": "Corporate Liquidations and Section 336/337/331 Consequences", "description": "This topic explains the tax consequences when a corporation winds up and distributes assets to shareholders.", "children": [{"id": "21a290fe-a523-4bf7-9d1e-31992d7e098d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Corporate-level effects", "children": [{"id": "1ea0e0e3-aec1-496a-9463-05a306fe7510", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 336"}, {"id": "15f159f4-53f2-4897-a872-994f00d88a4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Built-in gain and loss"}, {"id": "9bef49e4-88e5-44d1-ae52-ccb02e283ae0", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations on loss recognition"}], "description": "Liquidation generally causes corporate recognition of gain or loss on distributed property."}, {"id": "6e2acfc4-527a-445f-a31f-b366f14a0572", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shareholder effects", "children": [{"id": "84b7f525-2667-435e-ad09-71231602c227", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 331"}, {"id": "5bb8e8a1-20e6-4962-bdc5-ecbb2c82ab07", "type": "concept", "title": "Amount realized"}, {"id": "9cd80f85-01fc-49b1-83a5-49dde9a32405", "type": "concept", "title": "Stock basis and capital gain or loss"}], "description": "Shareholders usually treat liquidation as an exchange of stock."}, {"id": "e3dbf873-71ff-4f1e-8ad8-8ceab2589d64", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Subsidiary liquidations", "children": [{"id": "d88caec1-e152-4429-a9d1-b4a9791c9619", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 332"}, {"id": "dedf0fe2-ab73-4848-823b-686bd4e9f47b", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 337"}, {"id": "644a757f-2aa3-406f-b229-796829c4ca53", "type": "concept", "title": "Basis carryover"}], "description": "Parent-subsidiary liquidations can be nonrecognition events."}]}, {"id": "04150503-3956-4702-b69d-7cc9edd508c2", "type": "topic", "title": "Corporate Reorganizations and Tax-Free Transaction Planning", "description": "Students study tax-deferred reorganizations and the policy limits on corporate restructuring.", "children": [{"id": "fb62b73c-661d-49c5-9fb3-2e4b6dd24acb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reorganization framework", "children": [{"id": "590e4561-dba9-4588-8469-ae524f092fa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 368"}, {"id": "837aef97-edb9-491f-bac2-9373a9d11c0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity of interest"}, {"id": "07b45493-06f7-475c-95c6-c916aaccb39f", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuity of business enterprise"}], "description": "Students learn why some restructurings are tax-deferred rather than taxable sales."}, {"id": "aa934636-b5d6-4ac3-8b62-518a2f236148", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Types of reorganizations", "children": [{"id": "2f6e875e-2f44-4ddd-a003-184cd3a5b4d2", "type": "concept", "title": "A, B, C, D, E, F, and G reorganizations"}, {"id": "4d67f61f-425b-46e0-92eb-23cfe174d632", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset and stock reorganizations"}, {"id": "9da40823-b2d3-4ee1-9ed3-4d382e1539eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Recapitalizations"}], "description": "Different statutory forms support different business transactions."}, {"id": "b2174b6a-8c64-426c-9ffd-b032ab3e8008", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Boot and limitations", "children": [{"id": "26ef2dbb-b8f2-4265-b3ef-b7282db8fe18", "type": "concept", "title": "Boot recognition"}, {"id": "c0a47ff3-4b15-4aba-ac80-f44cdbdd8f4c", "type": "concept", "title": "Basis and holding period"}, {"id": "c6e99fcb-f778-4526-b60e-68f41cacf7db", "type": "concept", "title": "Business purpose and step transaction doctrine"}], "description": "Tax-free does not always mean tax-free for every party."}]}, {"id": "8fe9bad6-7638-4083-98b2-a024a59b91eb", "type": "topic", "title": "Consolidated Returns, Affiliated Groups, and Intercompany Transactions", "description": "This module introduces consolidated federal income tax reporting for related corporations.", "children": [{"id": "cf38c8cd-383e-44dc-9d56-bd400385b140", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Affiliated groups", "children": [{"id": "b0e6e3f6-df87-4f41-a7e0-31ca05e599ea", "type": "concept", "title": "80 percent ownership tests"}, {"id": "873afbfb-385e-4a58-8113-6bfe5522b7fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Common parent"}, {"id": "131775af-6748-430a-b086-e3bc19302183", "type": "concept", "title": "Excluded corporations"}], "description": "Students learn which corporations may file one consolidated return."}, {"id": "b51ac563-354c-40b6-ac2f-4645528e49c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Consolidated return mechanics", "children": [{"id": "917d1e0c-a0bc-44ef-8b1a-eff9728b4ed8", "type": "concept", "title": "Separate taxable income"}, {"id": "d09d96cb-72b2-4067-b8aa-052d5f400e8b", "type": "concept", "title": "Consolidated taxable income"}, {"id": "3f182791-1d2c-44ad-a126-dee5c89b2d1c", "type": "concept", "title": "SRLY and loss limitation concepts"}], "description": "Consolidation changes how income, losses, and basis are measured."}, {"id": "703b3430-d624-471f-ae20-abd25a314344", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intercompany transactions", "children": [{"id": "99e348e5-14db-4e7f-ba36-cbab7e6269a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Intercompany sales"}, {"id": "7a9069eb-b1c8-430a-b582-97a4e003f95d", "type": "concept", "title": "Deferred gains"}, {"id": "c5696954-902d-48f0-95f0-1fbbd5e13660", "type": "concept", "title": "Basis adjustments"}], "description": "Related-party transactions require matching and deferral rules."}]}, {"id": "d236537d-71bc-4ef6-8dae-055d65dc7743", "type": "topic", "title": "S Corporations and Pass-Through Comparison", "description": "Students compare C corporations with S corporations to understand entity choice and shareholder taxation.", "children": [{"id": "33a5a9e2-5dc5-4a50-8974-ff93b6845437", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Eligibility and election", "children": [{"id": "324b5e4c-0746-42dd-9ee3-aadbd5815d07", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligible shareholders"}, {"id": "6dfb5974-bca0-4670-aa90-c2e9734985c3", "type": "concept", "title": "One class of stock"}, {"id": "0fcda6f4-ec6e-4712-901e-0f5b814bb1e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Election and termination"}], "description": "S corporation status is elective and limited."}, {"id": "0461f4bd-0cb0-494e-85f9-eb7439bf8f0f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shareholder taxation", "children": [{"id": "84339d2a-5e61-4d0f-811e-5da56d887c1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Stock and debt basis"}, {"id": "2857a56c-3ca3-4886-b9f7-be914b5d9cb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Loss limitations"}, {"id": "f22444a3-d4c3-4650-a796-2d8822f69e0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributions"}], "description": "S corporations pass income, loss, deductions, and credits through to owners."}, {"id": "9cc264f0-4243-4287-8116-1ee40a0127db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "C versus S comparison", "children": [{"id": "76f62ded-aac7-4628-969a-5607093d154c", "type": "concept", "title": "Entity choice"}, {"id": "abeae79d-f426-4d57-a101-5cf38cac606d", "type": "concept", "title": "Built-in gains tax"}, {"id": "4d3625dd-02b6-423a-bcf6-de18f8f9ad14", "type": "concept", "title": "Reasonable compensation"}], "description": "Students learn when double taxation is worth accepting and when pass-through treatment dominates."}]}, {"id": "92b37b45-e5aa-4628-b406-cf726ea91503", "type": "topic", "title": "Partnership Taxation Essentials for Entity Choice", "description": "This topic gives enough partnership tax to compare corporate and noncorporate structures intelligently.", "children": [{"id": "5b6a20b9-2f87-469a-8764-8a376c5cd9f9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Formation and basis", "children": [{"id": "8f301b37-2e35-4415-a1e8-6cdfaf8147bf", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 721"}, {"id": "44050a76-d772-4607-bf8f-4fd780161093", "type": "concept", "title": "Outside and inside basis"}, {"id": "6ea32615-409a-4e48-b5ff-cc7fdcd28378", "type": "concept", "title": "Liabilities and basis"}], "description": "Partnership tax uses outside basis, inside basis, and capital accounts."}, {"id": "452b255b-64d2-4c0a-a780-5d8cc32422c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Allocations and distributions", "children": [{"id": "967ef8e3-71ae-496b-bbad-f10dcc4bf039", "type": "concept", "title": "Substantial economic effect"}, {"id": "ca9324a6-3249-434f-bf5d-fac4276bad10", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributions"}, {"id": "bdc540be-42e4-4aab-b530-d76ceaa26567", "type": "concept", "title": "Hot assets preview"}], "description": "Partnerships allow flexible economic sharing subject to anti-abuse rules."}, {"id": "79ff3164-5327-436b-a88f-ba2b0265f1d7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparison to corporations", "children": [{"id": "c3102c03-7d68-4f03-8575-86971311067d", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-level tax"}, {"id": "01b8e9d1-92be-4846-8a5b-ebc65a0f8553", "type": "concept", "title": "Special allocations"}, {"id": "75bbec7b-5abb-47c6-98e2-1b69eb548e49", "type": "concept", "title": "Exit and liquidation differences"}], "description": "Students learn how partnership flexibility contrasts with corporate double tax."}]}, {"id": "7b554aab-b8c3-4fbf-bd13-6d5f158b0fee", "type": "topic", "title": "Mergers, Acquisitions, Spin-Offs, and Transaction Structuring", "description": "Students apply corporate tax rules to deals, asset/stock acquisitions, section 338 elections, and divisive transactions.", "children": [{"id": "952c0533-b7e4-4579-b3ed-160c9392f9c1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Acquisition structure", "children": [{"id": "92dcd1e3-6ab5-4337-b9c1-bd110816cd3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset acquisitions"}, {"id": "1a02c43c-cc07-4cfc-82ce-e73489c31dfd", "type": "concept", "title": "Stock acquisitions"}, {"id": "6b4427e5-8700-49a8-a514-3e6395a6e9c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Section 338 and 336(e) elections"}], "description": "Tax consequences differ sharply between asset and stock deals."}, {"id": "7eed2845-e3a3-4668-841d-434a96606258", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deal tax attributes", "children": [{"id": "1951c665-3998-41d7-a79f-1d9025b0c771", "type": "concept", "title": "Step-up in basis"}, {"id": "16e1454c-ce39-4ebf-917e-d4e8030d1edf", "type": "concept", "title": "NOL limitations under section 382"}, {"id": "bf4ea016-a3f6-409b-b093-16d018605046", "type": "concept", "title": "Transaction costs"}], "description": "Transactions reshape basis, earnings, losses